[Chapter "Traps"]
[Line "Don't take the bait: 3...Nd4"]
[Opening "Italian Game: Blackburne-Kostić Gambit"]

{Black leaves e5 hanging to set a trap. Don't grab it; just trade knights.} 1. e4 {Take the centre and open lines for the queen and the f1 bishop.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 {The Italian: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp.} 3... Nd4 {A trap: after 4.Nxe5? Qg5 the queen hits the knight and g2, and the natural 5.Nxf7? walks into a quick mating attack.} 4. Nxd4 {Just trade knights; no tricks.} 4... exd4 5. O-O {Castle. White is ahead in development, and the d4 pawn can become a target later.} *
